description:
Change under review: add text search and sorting to a customer's order list. Added files are shown in full. For changed files, only the changed region is shown; the rest of the file is unchanged and compiles.

`src/routes/orders.ts` (changed, lines 8-14):
```ts
8 app.get("/orders", requireSession, async (req) => {
9   const url = new URL(req.url);
10   const term = url.searchParams.get("q") ?? "";
11   const sort = url.searchParams.get("sort") ?? "newest";
12   const orders = await searchOrders(req.session.customerId, term, sort);
13   return Response.json(orders);
14 });
```

`src/db/orders.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import { sql } from "./client.js";
2 import type { Order } from "./types.js";
3
4 const SORT_COLUMNS: Record<string, string> = {
5   newest: "created_at DESC",
6   oldest: "created_at ASC",
7   largest: "total_cents DESC",
8 };
9
10 export async function searchOrders(customerId: string, term: string, sort: string): Promise<Order[]> {
11   const orderBy = Object.hasOwn(SORT_COLUMNS, sort) ? SORT_COLUMNS[sort] : SORT_COLUMNS.newest;
12   return await sql<Order[]>`
13     SELECT id, status, total_cents, created_at
14     FROM orders
15     WHERE customer_id = ${customerId}
16       AND note ILIKE ${"%" + term + "%"}
17     ORDER BY ${sql.unsafe(orderBy)}
18     LIMIT 50
19   `;
20 }
```

`sql` is the existing postgres.js client: a value interpolated into its tagged template is sent as a bound parameter, never as SQL text, and `sql.unsafe(text)` inserts `text` into the query as raw SQL. `requireSession` is the existing session middleware; it sets `req.session.customerId` from the signed session cookie.
